// 0.0.3 V06 std library: `os` module — process interface.
//
// Both functions are VM intrinsics: `args` needs the CLI to pass the
// trailing program arguments through to the VM, and `exit` must stop
// execution from inside a call chain (D8).
//
//     args = std.os.args();   // [string] of the program arguments, without argv[0]
//     std.os.exit(3);         // terminate the process with exit code 3
//
// `exit` never returns: execution stops immediately, so it is valid
// anywhere a `unit`-valued statement is.